<title>CROATIA: Bavarian bank to bolster investment in Croatia.</title>
<headline>Bavarian bank to bolster investment in Croatia.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Landestanstalt fur Aufbaufninanzierung Bank (LFA) struck a deal on Monday with the Croatian Bank for Reconstruction and Development (HBOR) to finance Bavarian firms investing in Croatia.</p>
<p>State television said the LFA would grant loans of up to 25 million German marks to individual, medium-sized Bavarian enterprises for long-term investments in the former Yugoslav republic.</p>
<p>HBOR would give logistical support to the project by bolstering and speeding up contacts between Bavarian and Croatian potential partners.</p>
<p>It could also provide money for Croatian firms dealing with German partners within the project, the television said.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
